{"assets":["/statement-assets/a345a07d78edd712602c5048289c3aa02caa725771a2c96f631f842e60e87c5b.png","/statement-assets/093c179ad4d9c5f60a7262639f8767a20d61754b06eaafed0be07aa32b1e3c20.png","/statement-assets/8f5c374328209e220960cf100994affdfe508f8a3e4d87a1b922fe95e8b7dbd2.png","/statement-assets/2389c997951734f8cd09b21097517b280dea8cd4710dcbbbbf9efbd7dbda04d5.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"452","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Magic Trick"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alex enjoys performing magic tricks. He has a trick that requires a deck of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cards. He has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" identical decks of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" different cards each, which have been mixed together. When Alex wishes to perform the trick, he grabs "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cards at random and performs the trick with those. The resulting deck looks like a normal deck, but may have duplicates of some cards."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The trick itself is performed as follows: first Alex allows you to choose a random card from the deck. You memorize the card and put it back in the deck. Then Alex shuffles the deck, and pulls out a card. If the card matches the one you memorized, the trick is successful."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You don't think Alex is a very good magician, and that he just pulls a card randomly from the deck. Determine the probability of the trick being successful if this is the case."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First line of the input consists of two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":"), separated by space — number of cards in each deck, and number of decks."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On the only line of the output print one floating point number – probability of Alex successfully performing the trick. Relative or absolute error of your answer should not be higher than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0.6666666666666666\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0.4000000000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1.0000000000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, with probability "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a345a07d78edd712602c5048289c3aa02caa725771a2c96f631f842e60e87c5b.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" Alex will perform the trick with two cards with the same value from two different decks. In this case the trick is guaranteed to succeed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"With the remaining "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/093c179ad4d9c5f60a7262639f8767a20d61754b06eaafed0be07aa32b1e3c20.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" probability he took two different cards, and the probability of pulling off the trick is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/8f5c374328209e220960cf100994affdfe508f8a3e4d87a1b922fe95e8b7dbd2.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The resulting probability is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/2389c997951734f8cd09b21097517b280dea8cd4710dcbbbbf9efbd7dbda04d5.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"452C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/452/problem/C"}